WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.874
A system searches, reads its top results,

00:00:03.894 --> 00:00:06.078
builds a different query, and searches

00:00:06.098 --> 00:00:09.299
again. A model may help choose the words.

00:00:09.461 --> 00:00:11.052
Is this agentic search?

00:00:11.214 --> 00:00:14.429
Pause and ask a more precise question: who

00:00:14.449 --> 00:00:16.425
decided that another search would happen?

00:00:18.839 --> 00:00:21.101
Two pass pseudo relevance feedback can

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:23.614
follow exactly that prescribed sequence

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:26.539
every time. Its query contents adapt to

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.769
the first ranking while its next action

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:31.655
stays fixed. Result dependent content does

00:00:31.675 --> 00:00:35.985
not, by itself, establish agentic control.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.928
A fixed workflow follows a prescribed

00:00:38.948 --> 00:00:41.712
sequence. An adaptive workflow selects

00:00:41.732 --> 00:00:44.714
among branches explicitly enumerated by

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:48.438
its designer. A rule, classifier or model

00:00:48.458 --> 00:00:49.933
may choose that branch.

00:00:50.095 --> 00:00:52.176
Using a model for the choice does not

00:00:52.196 --> 00:00:53.515
settle the category.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.968
Agentic search lets a model plan at least

00:00:56.988 --> 00:00:59.288
part of a multi action retrieval

00:00:59.308 --> 00:01:01.401
trajectory from the task and its

00:01:01.421 --> 00:01:03.824
observations. Its tools are predefined

00:01:03.844 --> 00:01:06.053
too. The distinction is whether it

00:01:06.073 --> 00:01:08.759
assembles a sequence, rather than only

00:01:08.779 --> 00:01:11.130
selecting enumerated branches.

00:01:12.021 --> 00:01:15.169
The task brief supplies scope, criteria,

00:01:15.318 --> 00:01:18.378
sources, coverage, stopping conditions and

00:01:18.398 --> 00:01:19.537
the required record.

00:01:19.726 --> 00:01:22.347
The harness defines available operations,

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.530
reachable sources, budgets and limits.

00:01:25.705 --> 00:01:28.404
A tool means a callable operation, such as

00:01:28.424 --> 00:01:31.200
searching or fetching references, rather

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:33.055
than an entire licensed product.

00:01:33.613 --> 00:01:36.126
The model works within those permissions.

00:01:36.327 --> 00:01:38.845
Further reasoning cannot supply an

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.345
unavailable operation or inaccessible

00:01:41.365 --> 00:01:42.208
source.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:45.436
Output format is a separate property.

00:01:45.598 --> 00:01:48.413
A scripted deep search can return records

00:01:48.433 --> 00:01:49.972
after repeated retrieval.

00:01:50.134 --> 00:01:53.310
An agentic search can also return records.

00:01:53.472 --> 00:01:56.210
Either fixed or model planned retrieval

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.727
can precede a generated report or answer.

00:02:00.262 --> 00:02:03.079
Length, fluency and citations show

00:02:03.099 --> 00:02:05.991
generation, not who controlled the search.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.354
Basic RAG retrieves then generates.

00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:12.216
Agentic RAG lets a model choose retrieval

00:02:12.236 --> 00:02:14.483
actions towards a generated response;

00:02:14.749 --> 00:02:17.345
agentic search is broader and need not

00:02:17.365 --> 00:02:18.671
generate prose.

00:02:19.555 --> 00:02:21.847
Hybrid describes contributing retrieval

00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:24.360
routes. Multi stage describes how

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.898
operations follow earlier outputs.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.209
Agentic describes who chose the sequence.

00:02:30.372 --> 00:02:33.135
These properties can combine, but none

00:02:33.155 --> 00:02:35.609
automatically establishes the others.

00:02:36.171 --> 00:02:38.994
Model planned repeated BM twenty five

00:02:39.014 --> 00:02:41.675
searches can be agentic without being

00:02:41.695 --> 00:02:45.282
hybrid. Fixed lexical and dense retrieval

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:48.221
followed by fusion can be hybrid and multi

00:02:48.241 --> 00:02:50.579
stage without being agentic.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.770
The controller changes which operations

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:55.863
run; it does not change BM twenty five’s

00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:57.151
scoring formula.

00:02:58.055 --> 00:02:59.856
The chapter’s April twenty twenty six

00:02:59.876 --> 00:03:03.194
account places Asta Find Paper in a semi

00:03:03.214 --> 00:03:06.235
rigid, predefined flow shaped by model

00:03:06.255 --> 00:03:08.735
decisions. It contrasts Undermind’s

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:11.686
original deep search with Projects, which

00:03:11.706 --> 00:03:14.366
the account describes as dynamically

00:03:14.386 --> 00:03:16.685
selecting and chaining tools.

00:03:17.218 --> 00:03:19.268
These are dated reference points along a

00:03:19.288 --> 00:03:22.103
continuum, not new product tests.

00:03:22.278 --> 00:03:24.655
One vendor can offer different control

00:03:24.675 --> 00:03:26.561
arrangements in different modes.

00:03:26.711 --> 00:03:29.822
Iteration or a model inside a pipeline is

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.129
insufficient evidence of an independently

00:03:32.149 --> 00:03:33.456
planned trajectory.

00:03:34.378 --> 00:03:36.467
An April twenty twenty six Web of Science

00:03:36.487 --> 00:03:39.727
Research Assistant post used fully agentic

00:03:39.748 --> 00:03:42.021
while describing automatic choice among

00:03:42.041 --> 00:03:44.405
task routes. That description is

00:03:44.425 --> 00:03:47.034
compatible with adaptive control; the post

00:03:47.054 --> 00:03:49.161
does not settle whether novel sequences

00:03:49.181 --> 00:03:50.436
can be composed.

00:03:50.983 --> 00:03:53.789
It also documents user review and approval

00:03:53.809 --> 00:03:56.404
of a proposed strategy before retrieval,

00:03:56.618 --> 00:03:58.943
followed by an Advanced Search expression.

00:03:59.092 --> 00:04:01.314
That approval gate is a concrete control

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:03.968
property. It is different from deciding

00:04:04.015 --> 00:04:06.327
when an ongoing search has enough evidence

00:04:06.347 --> 00:04:07.254
to stop.

00:04:08.155 --> 00:04:10.261
For a known task with a sound established

00:04:10.281 --> 00:04:13.534
procedure, fixed or adaptive control may

00:04:13.554 --> 00:04:14.693
be the better bargain.

00:04:14.843 --> 00:04:16.949
Agentic control can attempt an

00:04:16.969 --> 00:04:19.501
unanticipated sequence using available

00:04:19.521 --> 00:04:22.658
actions, with added cost, latency and

00:04:22.678 --> 00:04:24.616
variation between runs.

00:04:25.159 --> 00:04:27.826
Inspect the required sequence, available

00:04:27.846 --> 00:04:31.280
actions and evidence of who chose the next

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.896
move. The next film examines why more

00:04:33.916 --> 00:04:36.370
iterations can preserve a blind spot just

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.509
as easily as repair one.
